@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Deployment: one durable host, local compiler, retained identity services
node "Student's device" <<device>> {
  node "Browser" as Browser <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Built React frontend\nunsaved drafts / native recorder" as React
    artifact "Optional read-aloud\nbrowser/OS voices" as Speech
  }
}
node "HTTPS reverse proxy" as Proxy <<executionEnvironment>>
node "Durable application host\nrestricted service account" <<device>> {
  node "FastAPI / Uvicorn / Python\nloopback or firewalled private interface" as Backend <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Backend + deterministic compiler\nlocal document extraction" as Python
    artifact "frontend/dist\nserved on the same origin" as Assets
    artifact "Server-only configuration\nSMTP / optional Google / storage" as Configuration
  }
  node "Persistent private disk" <<device>> {
    artifact "auth.sqlite3" as Accounts
    artifact "workspaces/<account UUID>/workspace.sqlite3\ncoursework + screenshot rows included" as Workspace
    artifact "Per-account audio / verified backups" as PrivateFiles
  }
  artifact "Versioned dictionary / constructed practice\nread-only reference sources" as Reference
}
node "Protected off-host backup destination" as Recovery <<external storage>>
node "Microphone / speakers" as Devices <<device>>
node "Google OAuth / signing keys" as Google <<external service>>
node "SMTP provider" as Mail <<external service>>
node "Optional browser-selected voice service\nimplementation-dependent" as VoiceService <<external service>>
Browser -- Proxy : HTTPS: frontend and private APIs
Proxy -- Backend : restricted HTTP;\ntrusted forwarded headers
Python ..> Accounts : identity transactions
Python ..> Workspace : account/project-selected transactions
Python ..> PrivateFiles : locked media / recovery operations
Python ..> Reference : read-only lookup
Backend -- Recovery : operator-managed consistent snapshots
Browser -- Devices : permissioned recording / playback
Browser -- Google : optional human authorization
Backend -- Google : optional HTTPS code exchange / JWT validation
Backend -- Mail : configured account email via STARTTLS
Browser -- VoiceService : only if browser TTS implementation uses it
Configuration ..> Python
legend bottom
  No language-model, OCR or transcription integration exists.
  Google/SMTP are network identity services; local compilation is not a claim of an offline website.
  Local development: browser -> loopback FastAPI; no public proxy needed.
  Authentication stays enabled; legacy CSV/profile/screenshots are a separate maintenance boundary.
  Backup identity/configuration separately from user ZIPs. Account isolation is not E2E encryption.
  Do not deploy private SQLite to ephemeral disks or imply a multi-host database cluster.
endlegend
@enduml
